[{:db/id "q-15479/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "1f0ca27e-b43a-59d9-b50d-713673aeff1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15479/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "42273e68-e32b-54b0-b2af-9d895f8d8bcb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15479/selection/71b1db0b2a675655ec27a2d2ceef2e86712a68eb78548232215378e0a354fb4c" :answer/id #uuid "b42176ef-174e-5805-88ab-84857c192b62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15479/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "71187d4a-22f1-599d-99ed-a5664a0f98f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15479/selection/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" :answer/id #uuid "49bce016-19b0-5418-a632-3e4a4a465f6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15479/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8101ebe3-8ace-5fc9-9b0f-a5d20dd4fce9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-15479/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-15479/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-15479/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-15479/selection/71b1db0b2a675655ec27a2d2ceef2e86712a68eb78548232215378e0a354fb4c" "q-15479/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-15479/selection/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-15479" :question/id #uuid "79a56d13-19ce-5345-b6e6-3de7b06f4714" :question/math-academy-id "q-15479" :question/problem "What is the coefficient of $(x+1)^{3}$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ about $x=-1?$" :question/worked-solution "The coefficient of $(x+1)^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{(3)}(-1).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-\\frac{24}{{x}^{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{‴}(-1),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{‴}(-1)=-\\frac{24}{(-1)^{5}}=-\\frac{24}{(-1)}=24.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(-1)=\\frac{1}{3!}\\cdot 24=\\frac{24}{6}=4.\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of $(x+1)^{3}$ is $4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-15479/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dc0250e-2aa9-5439-b567-93a59fa1c364"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-15479"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-15484"] :question/problem "What is the coefficient of $(x+\\pi )^{3}$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ about $x=-\\pi ?$" :question/worked-solution "The coefficient of $(x+\\pi )^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{(3)}(-\\pi ).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{‴}(-\\pi ),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{‴}(-\\pi )=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(-\\pi )=\\frac{1}{3!}\\cdot 1=\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of $(x+\\pi )^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{6}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-126359/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "aab72c3b-3e42-516f-81fc-8d253ba110c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126359/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "e28d33c6-9b54-5018-8c30-20b4328565a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126359/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "377d4d07-1be2-5ae5-a838-0cd5db52bc19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126359/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "f64f7624-f5e2-5746-81d4-517943568d06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126359/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "4ab1012d-433c-5c61-b762-c95a6cfddbbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126359/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3cd34680-796d-5b2d-a195-fe32a22dd5ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-126359/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-126359/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" "q-126359/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-126359/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-126359/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-126359/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-126359" :question/id #uuid "384d449f-273e-593f-9d4d-a9fdf55ff2d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-126359" :question/problem "What is the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{1-x}$ about $x=0?$" :question/worked-solution "The coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{(3)}(0).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{1-x} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{(1-x)^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{2}{(1-x)^{3}} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =\\frac{6}{(1-x)^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{‴}(0),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{‴}(0)=\\frac{6}{(1-0)^{4}}=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(0)=\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 6=1.\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is $1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-126359/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dc0250e-2aa9-5439-b567-93a59fa1c364"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126359"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351859/field-1/caf0ae0eff7086b036561e21b2f231ad088090f8ab18b31c3509b39b56285f9a" :answer/id #uuid "3ba2eba6-98da-551a-a9d7-eaba0126d0c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x^2-\\frac{4}{3}x^3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351859/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f2a61a26-d697-50e5-9a14-f09ca5b0e334" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351859/field-1/caf0ae0eff7086b036561e21b2f231ad088090f8ab18b31c3509b39b56285f9a" :answer-field/choices ["q-351859/field-1/caf0ae0eff7086b036561e21b2f231ad088090f8ab18b31c3509b39b56285f9a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351859" :question/id #uuid "783fb36c-345a-5c94-9d91-f565c09ac763" :question/math-academy-id "q-351859" :question/problem "Find the third-degree Taylor polynomial ${P}_{3}(x)$ of $f(x)={e}^{-2x}$ about $x=0.$\n\n${P}_{3}(x)=1-2x\\,+$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the third-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=0,$ we plug $a=0$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!} \\\\  & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to compute $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={e}^{-2x} & ⟹ &  & f(0) & ={e}^{-0}=1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-2{e}^{-2x} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(0) & =-2{e}^{-0}=-2 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =4{e}^{-2x} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(0) & =4{e}^{-0}=4 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-8{e}^{-2x} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(0) & =-8{e}^{-0}=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we plug the results for $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0)$ into our third-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =1-2\\cdot x+4\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-8\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{6} \\\\  & =1-2x+2{x}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-351859/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9ea3dac-cf0a-5d05-8d77-7280ce9b5a94"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351859"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351980/field-1/e7f6c27482797e11bd6b0013338edc6789517ab47eb94f4fe9912fc5f8b6c4b8" :answer/id #uuid "fce4228c-cfb9-5019-80e2-cc10096c0284" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351980/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e10cb6b6-68f5-50a6-9f85-97dc918b5cc0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351980/field-1/e7f6c27482797e11bd6b0013338edc6789517ab47eb94f4fe9912fc5f8b6c4b8" :answer-field/choices ["q-351980/field-1/e7f6c27482797e11bd6b0013338edc6789517ab47eb94f4fe9912fc5f8b6c4b8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351980/field-2/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "55dfc2a7-a4a6-59e8-afc2-ff10a44550da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351980/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "c856bb87-8e3b-5471-8c50-c413f3aba9de" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351980/field-2/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer-field/choices ["q-351980/field-2/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351980/field-3/08871fb7631b7fd2bb61ad032d007534b5615919401e6794e5d258ae0ae13e58" :answer/id #uuid "ee32e8c8-f24c-58ef-bd1b-19c51dfa1a79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351980/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "a6a6fde1-b724-52d0-849e-f48493caa0a0" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351980/field-3/08871fb7631b7fd2bb61ad032d007534b5615919401e6794e5d258ae0ae13e58" :answer-field/choices ["q-351980/field-3/08871fb7631b7fd2bb61ad032d007534b5615919401e6794e5d258ae0ae13e58"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351980" :question/id #uuid "da23cd02-a4af-5514-bd1d-fc11e7c72462" :question/math-academy-id "q-351980" :question/problem "Find the third-degree Taylor polynomial ${P}_{3}(x)$ of $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ about $x=0.$ Do  not round the answer.\n\n${P}_{3}(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n$x\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}\n${x}^{3}$" :question/worked-solution "To find the third-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=0,$ we plug $a=0$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!} \\\\  & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to compute $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & ⟹ &  & f(0) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(0) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(0) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(0) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we plug the results into our Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}x+(-\\frac{1}{2})\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{12}{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-351980/field-1" "q-351980/field-2" "q-351980/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9ea3dac-cf0a-5d05-8d77-7280ce9b5a94"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351980"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
